  #line-at(304.8pt, 214.2pt, "redesigning the heating system. ")
  #line-at(314.76pt, 225.96pt, "An effective alternative to enhance microwave heating ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 237.72pt, "uniformity in a cavity is covering a metasurface on its wall ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 249.48pt, "[15], [16]. Metasurfaces are artificial subwavelength 2-D ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 261.24pt, "planar ")
  #line-at(340.91pt, 261.24pt, "structures ")
  #line-at(390.441pt, 261.24pt, "that ")
  #line-at(416.806pt, 261.24pt, "can ")
  #line-at(441.991pt, 261.24pt, "manipulate ")
  #line-at(497.031pt, 261.24pt, "and ")
  #line-at(522.723pt, 261.24pt, "control ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 273pt, "electromagnetic (EM) waves [17] - [23]. Our previous work ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 284.64pt, "demonstrated that a randomly arranged 1-bit coding ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 296.52pt, "metasurface can enhance the uniformity of the field inside the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 308.28pt, "cavity [15].  ")
  #line-at(314.76pt, 319.92pt, "In this letter, a 2-bit coding metasurface operating at ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 331.68pt, "2.45 GHz is designed to improve heating uniformity in a ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 343.44pt, "microwave cavity. By designing a unit cell with a period of ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 355.2pt, "only 0.08 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(348.96pt, 355.2pt, "λ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(353.16pt, 355.2pt, "₀ (the wavelength of the center frequency) and ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 366.96pt, "optimizing the elements arrangement via a genetic algorithm ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 378.72pt, "(GA), the EM waves incident on the metasurface can be ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 390.48pt, "scattered into multiple directions rather than just one. The ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 402.24pt, "uniformity of the field distribution in the cavity is significantly ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 414pt, "improved, thereby enhancing the heating uniformity. Good ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 425.76pt, "agreements between the measurements and simulations ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 437.4pt, "validate this improvement. This novel metasurface-based ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 449.28pt, "method requires neither redesign of the cavity nor ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 461.04pt, "modification of power excitation and can be employed in any ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 472.68pt, "rectangular heating cavity operating at 2.45 GHz. ")
