#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 494pt), 46pt, 90.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(545.28pt, 65.88pt, "2 ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 77.16pt, "> REPLACE THIS LINE WITH YOUR MANUSCRIPT ID NUMBER (DOUBLE-CLICK HERE TO EDIT) < ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 415.68pt, "cavity boundary by placing a metasurface on its wall. EM ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 427.56pt, "waves incident on metasurfaces satisfy the generalized Snell's ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 439.2pt, "law [26], enabling the metasurface to scatter the incident ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 450.96pt, "waves into multiple directions rather than just one, thereby ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 462.72pt, "resulting in enhanced uniformity of the field distribution. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.6pt, 480.36pt, "A. Elements Design and Arrangement ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.44pt, 494.4pt, "Considering that 2-bit coding offers greater flexibility in ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 506.28pt, "manipulating EM waves compared to 1-bit coding [27], a 2-bit ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 517.92pt, "coding metasurface is proposed to modify the boundary in a ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 529.68pt, "microwave heating cavity. This 2-bit coding metasurface ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 541.44pt, "composes of 2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.307pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.12pt, 537.96pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(111.24pt, 541.44pt, " elements: ′00′, ′01′, ′10′, and ′11′, which ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 553.2pt, "correspond to relative phase responses of 0, π/2, π, and 3π/2, ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 564.96pt, "respectively, thereby ensuring the four states cover a full 2π ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 576.72pt, "phase range. By arranging these elements in specific ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 588.48pt, "sequences, the scattering pattern of EM waves is flexibly ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 600.12pt, "controlled. The design diagram is summarized in Fig. 1. ")
  #line-at(55.44pt, 611.88pt, "Current designs of coding metasurfaces for EM scattering ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 623.76pt, "are primarily used for radar cross section (RCS) reduction. ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 635.4pt, "Metallic patch and square ring have been frequently used as ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 647.16pt, "the unit cells structure with a period of about 0.2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(245.04pt, 647.16pt, "λ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.24pt, 647.16pt, "₀ and even ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 659.04pt, "0.5 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(60.72pt, 659.04pt, "λ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(64.92pt, 659.04pt, "₀ [27], [28]. However, these elaborated designs cannot be ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 670.68pt, "directly applied for microwave heating in a 2.45 GHz cavity ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 682.44pt, "due to constraints posed by the cavity’s dimensions and the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 694.2pt, "unit cell size. In this work, a 2-bit coding metasurface design ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 705.96pt, "is proposed for the specific cavity dimensions (291 mm × ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 717.72pt, "291 mm × 186 mm) with a metasurface size of 180 mm × ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 729.48pt, "180 mm.  ")
  #line-at(55.44pt, 741.24pt, "Considering that flexible control of EM waves demands ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 752.88pt, "enough elements [28], the metasurface is composed of 6 × 6 ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 231.24pt, "elements with each containing 3 × 3 unit cells to mitigate ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 243.12pt, "phase distortions. The period of unit cells is, thus, set as ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 254.76pt, "10 mm, corresponding to 0.08 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(434.64pt, 254.76pt, "λ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(438.84pt, 254.76pt, "₀. The unit cells of square ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 266.52pt, "patch and ring with limited structural parameters, cannot ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 278.4pt, "provide the required phase responses for 2-bit coding ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 290.04pt, "metasurface with this small period. Therefore, a novel ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 301.8pt, "structure is introduced, incorporating a square ring with a ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 313.68pt, "cross and four L-shaped branches in the metallic patterned ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 325.32pt, "layer, as illustrated in Fig. 2. A ground plane is separated from ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 337.08pt, "the patterned layer by a 16 mm air gap. The metallic patterns ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 348.84pt, "are printed on a 1 mm-thick F4B dielectric substrate with a ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 360.6pt, "dielectric constant of 2.65 and a loss tangent of 0.001. By ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 372.36pt, "adjusting the structural parameters, the desired phase ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 384.12pt, "responses are achieved, as shown in Fig. 3 (a). To maximize ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 395.88pt, "the dispersion of scattered EM energy in various directions ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 407.52pt, "and enhance the field distribution uniformity within the cavity, ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 419.28pt, "GA is employed to optimize the arrangement of the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 431.16pt, "metasurface elements, and the result is illustrated in Fig. 3(b). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 448.68pt, "B. Uniformity Evaluation  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.76pt, 462.84pt, "To validate the proposed method, the E-field distributions ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 474pt, "in the microwave heating cavity with and without the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 485.16pt, "metasurface are simulated at 2.45 GHz. Fig. 4 (a) depicts the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 496.32pt, "cavity dimensions and the placement of the metasurface. For a ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 507.48pt, "clear comparison, the E-field (|")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(435.72pt, 507.48pt, "E")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(442.08pt, 507.48pt, "|) at 400,221 mesh points ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 518.76pt, "were exported and normalized by their average values. The ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 529.92pt, "probability density functions (PDFs) of the normalized E-field, ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 541.2pt, "presented in Fig. 4 (b), show that the points with E-field ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 552.36pt, "values close to the average are significantly more numerous in ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 563.52pt, "the cavity with the proposed metasurface than without it, ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 574.68pt, "indicating a substantial improvement in field uniformity. This ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 585.84pt, "improvement is illustrated by the total E-field distribution in ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 597.12pt, "Fig. 6 (a), where the metasurface eliminates the standing wave ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 608.28pt, "pattern observed in the cavity without the metasurface. ")
  #line-at(314.76pt, 619.56pt, "Further validation involved heating a piece of potato in the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 630.6pt, "cavity. Supported by a cubic glass with a dielectric constant of ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 641.88pt, "4 [29], the dimensions of the potato and glass are shown in ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 653.04pt, "Fig. 4 (a). The temperature distribution in the potato is ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 664.32pt, "simulated using COMSOL Multiphysics 6.0 [12], with the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 675.48pt, "relative permittivity of the potato modeled as a function of ")
