  #line-at(55.44pt, 445.08pt, "The COV without the metasurface is 0.694, which ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 456.72pt, "decreases to 0.461, 0.483, 0.425 and 0.524 with the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 468.48pt, "metasurface placed in front of the back, left, right and above ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 480.36pt, "walls, respectively (Fig. 6 (b)). The corresponding ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.96pt, 480.36pt, "T")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.307pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.36pt, 481.2pt, "avg")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(264.48pt, 480.36pt, " of the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 492pt, "potato with the metasurface is 24.4 °C, 26.7 °C, 20.5 °C, and ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 503.76pt, "28.3 °C, respectively, while ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(170.64pt, 503.76pt, "T")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.307pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.04pt, 504.72pt, "avg")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.16pt, 503.76pt, " is 24.6 °C without the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 515.52pt, "metasurface. The proposed method effectively improves ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 527.28pt, "heating uniformity without reducing the overall efficiency, ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 539.04pt, "except when the metasurface is placed right. In contrast, the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 550.68pt, "heating efficiency is enhanced when the metasurface is placed ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 562.56pt, "in front of the left and above walls, but with a little bit more ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 574.32pt, "hotspots (left) or less uniformity (above). In summary, ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 585.96pt, "considering COV, average temperature and hotspots, the ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 597.84pt, "optimal position for the metasurface is in front of the back ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 609.48pt, "wall. These differences in COV and average temperature are ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 621.24pt, "mainly caused by the asymmetric design of the metasurface.  ")
  #line-at(104.76pt, 644.76pt, "III.")
  #line-at(119.04pt, 644.76pt, "E")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.826pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.92pt, 644.76pt, "XPERIMENTAL ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.92pt, 644.76pt, "V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.826pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(188.88pt, 644.76pt, "ALIDATION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.44pt, 659.88pt, "To experimentally validate the proposed method, a ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 671.52pt, "microwave heating system is set up, as shown in Fig. 7. A ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 683.28pt, "fiber optic thermometer is used to measure the temperature at ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 695.04pt, "the center by inserting the fiber sensor into the potato and ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 706.8pt, "record the temperature once per second. An infrared thermal ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 718.56pt, "camera is used to immediately record the temperature ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 730.32pt, "distribution on the potato’s top surface after heating.  ")
  #line-at(55.44pt, 742.08pt, "Fig. 8 (a) illustrates the simulated and measured surface ")
  #line-at(45.6pt, 753.84pt, "temperature distributions. Good agreements are observed ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 365.4pt, "between them. The temperature distribution on the top surface ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 377.04pt, "becomes more uniform with the metasurface. Fig. 8 (b) ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 388.8pt, "compares the measured and simulated temporal variations of ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 400.68pt, "temperature at the potato center, with and without the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 412.32pt, "metasurface. The experimental data, representing the average ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 424.08pt, "temperature from three trials, closely matches the simulation. ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 435.84pt, "The discrepancies between the simulation and experimental ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 447.6pt, "results stem primarily from differences between the simulation ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 459.36pt, "model and the actual heating system.  ")
  #line-at(314.76pt, 471.12pt, "Although the temperature rise at the potato center is higher ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 482.88pt, "without the metasurface, the average temperature of the entire ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 494.64pt, "potato remains nearly the same, as indicated by the simulation ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 506.4pt, "results. This suggests that the proposed method effectively ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 518.16pt, "mitigates thermal runaway issues. ")
  #line-at(394.44pt, 541.56pt, "VI.")
  #line-at(409.2pt, 541.56pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.826pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(415.56pt, 541.56pt, "ONCLUSION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.695pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.76pt, 556.56pt, "This study proposes a method to improve heating ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 567.84pt, "uniformity in a cavity by introducing a metasurface operating ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 579pt, "at 2.45 GHz. This approach eliminates the need to redesign the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 590.16pt, "cavity or using multiple feeding sources. With the metasurface ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 601.44pt, "being less than 18 mm thick and positioned in front of the wall ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 612.48pt, "inside the cavity, the heating space is minimally impacted. The ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 623.76pt, "simulation results, including PDFs of the E-field and potato ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 634.92pt, "temperature, and COV of temperature, demonstrate significant ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 646.2pt, "improvement in heating uniformity, regardless of the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 657.36pt, "metasurface placement. Considering heating efficiency and ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 668.64pt, "hotspots, the optimal position can be identified. The simulated ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 679.68pt, "potato temperatures closely match the measured ones, ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 690.84pt, "validating the proposed method. Moreover, the proposed ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 702.12pt, "metasurface can be easily applied to other rectangular ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 713.28pt, "microwave heating cavities operating at 2.45 GHz. While the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 724.56pt, "narrow gap in the metasurface structure limits the power ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 735.72pt, "tolerance, the proposed method can find applications in a wide ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 746.88pt, "range of scenarios.  ")
